This licence covers PlayerOne's own source code only.

The release packages also contain mpv and ffmpeg, which are licensed under the
GNU General Public License. Those binaries are separate programs that PlayerOne
runs as child processes; no GPL code is linked into PlayerOne itself, which is
why PlayerOne's own source can carry this licence.

If you redistribute a package that bundles those binaries, the GPL obligations
travel with them. See docs/third-party.md for what that means in practice and
where the corresponding sources are.
